# GSD benchmark context

Read before changing harness, run workflow, or interpreting results:

1. **GSD commands:** [docs/GSD-COMMANDS.md](docs/GSD-COMMANDS.md) — invoke skills in Cursor; standard vs full catalog.
2. **GSD playbooks:** [docs/GSD-TUTORIAL-PLAYBOOKS.md](docs/GSD-TUTORIAL-PLAYBOOKS.md) — Case 1 greenfield PRD, Case 2 brownfield feature/bug.
3. **Experiment agenda:** [docs/EXPERIMENT-AGENDA.md](docs/EXPERIMENT-AGENDA.md) — three rungs (baseline / vanilla GSD / recipe), metrics, Feature A/B/C pilot.
4. **Product findings:** [docs/GSD-PRODUCT-CONTEXT.md](docs/GSD-PRODUCT-CONTEXT.md) — GSD limits and Cursor usage.
5. **Operator context:** [.planning/CONTEXT.md](.planning/CONTEXT.md) — arms, grader as DoD, scripts.
6. **Roadmap:** [.planning/ROADMAP.md](.planning/ROADMAP.md) — what to build next.

Do not treat GSD verify-work as passing the benchmark. Grade with `bench/grade/grade.sh` / `finalize-run.sh`. Recipe stamps measure process velocity; grader measures code quality.

**Never invoke GSD skills** (`gsd-new-project`, `gsd-plan-phase`, etc.) on behalf of the user. The user runs GSD manually; tutorial: [docs/GSD-TUTORIAL.md](docs/GSD-TUTORIAL.md).
